From 76a47a39f5d7e422d583bac64b8c8b2a58f718e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tasker <tasker@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:12:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] hw/audio: add intel-hda-ace, the Intel ACE 1.0 audio DSP
 (Arrow Lake-S 8086:7f50)

A variant of intel-hda for the Intel Smart Sound Technology BUS function of
Arrow Lake-S/HX: BAR0 is the controller as before (plus the capability
chain of the previous patches), BAR4 is the ACE 1.0 DSP bar with its
register block and two SRAM windows.  The model runs the boot handshake a
host driver exercises: the subsystem and core power-up (CPA follows SPA
after a model delay), the purge request and its DONE reply, the ROM state
walk to INIT_DONE, the code-loader stream consumed through QEMA DMA up to
the stream SPIB, the ROM judgement of the streamed .ri container (model
rules, with the 16 documented halt codes), the walk to FW_ENTERED, the
firmware register block and the FW_READY notification in window 0, the
IPC4 FW_CONFIG reply with its TLV list, and the controller-level
interrupt (INTSTS bit 30, INTx or MSI) gated by the BAR4 enables.  The
fault injector (property fault, QMP-settable), x-delay-scale, the
personality table of the six ACE 1.0 controllers and the powered-down read
value are the test hooks; every value the ABI does not dictate is a named
model value.

Sources studied (nothing copied; see intel-hda-ace-regs.h for the per-block
citations): Linux v6.12 sound/soc/sof/intel/mtl.h, hda.h, mtl.c,
hda-loader.c and include/sound/sof/ipc4/header.h (GPL-2.0-only OR
BSD-3-Clause; declarations re-derived under LICENSING.md rule 7); SOF
fcebbbf22d7 src/include/ipc4/{header.h,fw_reg.h,base_fw.h,notification.h,
error_status.h}, src/include/sof/tlv.h and rimage
tools/rimage/src/include/rimage/{cavs/cavs_ext_manifest.h,cse.h,
sof/user/manifest.h} (BSD-3); the .ri field offsets verified byte for
byte against the pinned sof-arl-s.ri (sof-firmware 2026.09.2, sha256
f37a055c...dc647c6e); the boot handshake as prose in the P2a/P2b NOTES
(facts).  The GPL-3 LiberNT driver and fake-DSP sources were not opened.
